  {
   "id": "development",
   "minutes": 10,
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "id": "dev_open",
     "text": "Mole-ratio steps are convention: watch one, try one, alone. Fertilizer: 1 mol \\ce{N2} : 3 mol \\ce{H2} means 6 kg \\ce{H2} ($3000$ mol) needs $1000$ mol (28 kg) \\ce{N2}."
    },
    {
     "type": "diagram",
     "spec": {
      "type": "chem_equation",
      "equation": "N2 + 3H2 -> 2NH3",
      "caption": "1:3:2 = mole ratio"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "diagram",
     "spec": {
      "type": "molecule",
      "smiles": "N",
      "formula": "NH3",
      "name": "ammonia",
      "caption": "ammonia, 2 mol formed"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "key_points",
     "items": [
      "Coefficients = mole ratio.",
      "Ratio comes from coefficients, not subscripts.",
      "Same ratio fixes particles, mass, STP volume."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "keywords",
     "items": [
      {
       "word": "mole ratio",
       "meaning": "ratio of moles from coefficients"
      },
      {
       "word": "coefficient",
       "meaning": "number in front of a formula"
      },
      {
       "word": "STP",
       "meaning": "1 mole of gas = $22.4$ dm³"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "latex",
     "tex": "\\dfrac{n(\\text{N}_2)}{n(\\text{H}_2)} = \\dfrac{1}{3}",
